; Release builds for Linux link statically against musl, so the binary runs
; on a machine with no OCaml, no wand tree and no matching libc. Static
; linking is a Linux-only idea -- macOS does not support it and does not need
; it -- so it lives in a profile the macOS jobs do not use. Scoped to this
; directory: the stdlib table's generator runs on the build machine and has
; no reason to be linked this way.

(env
 (static
  (link_flags
   (-ccopt -static))))

(executable
 (public_name wand)
 (name wand)
 (modules wand)
 (libraries wand))
